From a73e2a187bc9c4c7f2e5051705043f6fe430116b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Save pages to this machine: save.roots, save.queue,
 save.status, save.list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A queued save opens the page in a background tab, waits for the network to
go quiet, and writes MHTML (Page.captureSnapshot) and/or PDF into a folder
inside one of CHROMERS_SAVE_ROOTS (default web=~/Archive/web). Paths that
lead out of a root (.., absolute, symlinks) are refused; names come from
the page title and date, never overwriting ("… (2)"). One save at a time;
finished jobs are kept for save.status and appended to
~/.config/chromers/saves.jsonl. For the TaskDeck "Save web page" job.

Tested end to end with headless Chromium: MHTML includes JS-rendered
content and images; escape attempts, unknown roots and missing tokens
are refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
